{"kind":"request","text":"Checker: the design of the addressed-work and requester-acceptance lifecycle (request 9c43c173, N2; promise 6f1481eb), at exact head 7f49d9e4dbb96525a8f4ffa484d00078de4d3595 on request/work-item-lifecycle, cut from main e6e67828. One path: notes/2026-10-03-work-item-lifecycle.md, revision 4. It is a design for review and adoption; nothing in it is built or run, and it changes nothing in the release under review. Contents: the work item, the commitment and the hold kept apart, with the performer distinct from any holder; the actors, with a fixed requester and acceptor and three narrow admin powers; one record for an item (state, parties, offered and accepted terms, a versioned current commitment, report, transfer, outcome, revision); every transition with who, the state, further guards, its effect and what it never does, including the performer's explicit agreement to amended terms; one revision guard and both orders of each race; lease expiry, policy activation and the reserved-publication boundary. The destination is the enforced lifecycle: a general Room-owned thread record with declared guards and effects as data, under a new steps version (an unheld file step, a transition step, bounded fixed guard and effect forms, one admission step, party slots that only a passed transition sets, a signer guard checked as well as the role rule, refusals with the present state, notification intents chosen from the record before and after), the lifecycle written out as declarations in those forms, the meaning of an item's transitions pinned at filing by a definition identity with a compatibility rule and replay that derives effects, and the producer, read, verifier and policy validation named. A reduced cooperative practice on today's entry comments is kept as an option and is said not to enforce: its reading rule is pinned by identity, the Room's receipt is kept apart from the reading, and a gap or an unsupported act makes what follows unknown. Attent